//
// PROBE: the workbench forms of three string and conversion words, and the
// case-folding de-duplication of `string.tokenize.unique`.
//
// Each `.` form takes its operand from the workbench, and they do not agree on
// where the result goes:
//
//   - `string.tokenize.lines.` and `string.tokenize.unique.` pull from the
//     workbench and push to the **stack**: their shared base pushes with
//     `vm.stack.push` whatever the operand source
//     (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/string/tokenize.rs:94,108).
//   - `string.expressionmatch.` takes the expression from the workbench and
//     the subject from the stack, and leaves its answer on the **workbench**
//     (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/string/textexpr_match.rs:29,33,67).
//   - `convert.to_textbuffer.` converts on the workbench and leaves the result
//     there (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/convert/internal.rs:56-58).
//
// `string.tokenize.unique` lowercases and collects into a `HashSet`
// (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/string/tokenize.rs:49-50), so the
// order of its tokens changes from run to run. The input here has one distinct
// token, which is the only shape a golden can hold.
//
"probe: string.tokenize.lines. takes the workbench and pushes to the stack" println
"one
  two
three" . string.tokenize.lines. println
"probe: string.tokenize.unique folds case and removes duplicates" println
"Word word WORD" string.tokenize.unique println
"Word word WORD" . string.tokenize.unique. println
"probe: string.expressionmatch. answers on the workbench" println
"the answer is 42" 'contains "42"' . string.expressionmatch. debug.display_workbench
"probe: convert.to_textbuffer. converts on the workbench" println
42 . convert.to_textbuffer. debug.display_workbench
